    "All binary values are lowercase hex unless the field name says b64url (RFC 4648 §5, no padding).",
    "envelope = nonce (12 bytes) || AES-256-GCM ciphertext || tag (16 bytes); nonce = direction (4 bytes BE) || counter (8 bytes BE).",
    "aad is the UTF-8 of the HTTP method, one space and the request target as sent: the path and, if any, the query.",
    "A reply uses the downstream key and the aad of the request it answers.",
    "hkdf salt is the 32 token bytes (not their base64url text); info is the UTF-8 of kario-switch/1.",
    "The pairing URL query is form-encoded (Go's url.Values.Encode): + is a space.",
    "The hello reply is what the receiver sends when its random source gives the receiver's private key, the token and 8 zero bytes (the session id)."
